<title>HUNGARY: Rising Hungarian, Polish shares push CESI higher.</title>
<headline>Rising Hungarian, Polish shares push CESI higher.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The CESI Central European Share Index firmed on Wednesday to close at 1,393.20 points, up 1.71 points or 0.12 percent, the Budapest Stock Stock Exchange said.</p>
<p>The rise of the index triggered by price rises in Budapest and Warsaw.</p>
<p>The index, which has been published since February 1, reflects trends of 50 shares on the Budapest, Prague and Warsaw bourses.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327-4040</p>
</text>
